# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit .env files (they are git-ignored).
#
# Rules
# - Secrets (API keys, tokens, passwords) never go in code or in this file with real values.
#   Add them in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables, per environment
#   (Production / Preview / Development).
# - Only variables prefixed with VITE_ reach the browser, and anything that reaches the
#   browser is public: anyone can read it in the built JavaScript. Never put a secret in a
#   VITE_ variable. Real secrets need a server (for example a Vercel Function), which this
#   prototype does not have.
# - Read them in code with import.meta.env.VITE_NAME.
#
# The prototype needs no variables today. Example of a public, non-secret value:
# VITE_APP_ENV=local
